Original commit body from fdc44718300a633d2cff9674e177cf3303640966:

THE STEP READER LISTED A STEP THE LOG FETCHER COULD NOT REACH. On dev
8955d9a2 -- push/woodpecker beside the hand-triggered cron/full-suite
pipeline 2206, both green -- `ci-debug status` rendered self-claims-gate
under the cron gate (INV-bozid's per-step reader), and `ci-debug logs
self-claims-gate 8955d9a2` answered "Nothing named 'self-claims-gate' on
this commit -- no gate and no step by that name" and printed the PUSH
pipeline's transcript. Listing and fetching disagreed about what exists,
and INV-bofab's closure evidence had to rest on a construction argument
(check-self-claims exits 2 on infra failure, non-zero on drift) instead
of the transcript itself.

THE MECHANISM, FROM THE FETCHER'S OWN COMMENT. WI-zavut made the job name
select a GATE by context (full or trailing segment) and, failing that,
fall back to the failed gate or the first one -- before any step was
consulted. A step name matches no context, so for every step on a sibling
gate rule 2 had already chosen the wrong pipeline by the time the step
selector ran, and the honest substitution warning (INV-vazuh) then
reported a step as absent that the same tool had just listed.

THE FIX. When the name matches no gate and credentials are present, every
gate's pipeline is read (failed gates first, mirroring rule 2) and the
first one carrying a step of that name chooses the pipeline; the existing
step selector then matches it and no warning fires. The genuinely-absent
case keeps the warning, and it is honest only because every pipeline was
searched before it fires -- pinned by the control test, which asserts both
pipeline reads precede the substitution line. The loop is a `while ...
done <<<` in the calling shell so its assignments survive (the
WP_HTTP_CODE lesson, one function up).

THE HARNESS HAD DRIFTED. tests/_forge_github_harness.py's fake curl claims
to mirror test_forge_backend_github.py's and printed the HTTP code ALONE
when no -o was given, so the first green-path log fetch through it parsed
"200" as the log body ("returned int, not a log-entry list"). It now emits
body then code for -w as real curl does; all 72 tests across the nine
harness consumers pass unchanged.

LIVE REPRO, RE-RUN WITH THE FIX: `ci-debug logs self-claims-gate 8955d9a2`
returns the cron gate's 485-line transcript with no substitution line,
ending "check-self-claims-drift: OK -- 18 claims unchanged (18
confirmed_with_caveats)" -- the transcript INV-bofab's closure note named
as unread.

